Alisha: Quick heads-up — I opened a docs PR (https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/3421) that rewrites the streaming examples to use iterator-style consumers across Python/TS/Go. The preview is rendering but the pagination + retry wording might be misleading. Can someone eyeball the semantics before I merge?

Devon: I skimmed it — main change looks good. For Python we switched from the old callback pattern to:```python
for chunk in client.stream_generate(...):
    if chunk.retry_after:
        # backoff handling
        continue
    handle(chunk)
```
Need to call out that `retry_after` is advisory (not a blocking retry).

Marta: Nice. On TS we used an async iterator:```ts
for await (const part of client.stream.create(...)) {
  if (part.error) {
    // don't throw; surface to caller for custom backoff
  }
  display(part)
}
```
We probably should add a tiny note about client-side buffering and that pagination tokens are separate from streaming cursors.

Alisha: Good point — I added a short paragraph but it's terse. Would be great to have a 1-sentence explicit distinction: "streaming yields tokens/chunks; pagination yields discrete pages via next_token".

Sam: I'll add a short section explaining mechanical retries vs user-level retries. Proposal: show a small example that uses exponential backoff when `part.error?.code === 'RATE_LIMIT'`. Keep it language-agnostic then link to per-SDK snippet.

Devon: One more thing — Go snippet currently uses a channel + goroutine; I refactored to a blocking iterator to simplify:```go
for resp := range client.Stream(ctx, req) {
  if resp.Err != nil {
    // surface and let caller decide
    continue
  }
  process(resp.Part)
}
```
Add comment that users should not spawn unbounded goroutines for each stream.

Marta: I found two broken links in the migration guide referencing the old `stream()` method name. I pushed a tiny fix to the PR that updates both anchors and adds a redirect note.

docs-bot: Preview deployed — https://docs-preview.redwood.ai/pr-3421 — status: build passed :white_check_mark:

Alisha: Thanks all. Action items: Sam to add the retry snippet (small, crosslang) by EOD, Devon to annotate Go note, Marta to confirm link fix, I'll squash and merge once green. If anyone wants a final pass ping me :wave:
